# Zyko's PC Checker 4 — Terms of Use
Effective September 20, 2026. Applies with the attribution-preserving LICENSE.

Use the software only on devices and data you are authorized to examine. Before
examining another person's device, explain the chosen scope, the types of data
collected, who will receive the report, the retention period and how to contact
the operator. Obtain informed permission or establish other valid authority.
The expanded-scan acknowledgement records an operator choice; it does not itself
establish permission from the device owner. Declining expanded collection must
not be represented as evidence of cheating.

Expanded collection can reveal sensitive commands, network activity, identifiers,
file history and system settings. The optional memory inspection has additional
access requirements. Review the Privacy Policy before enabling these features.
Protect local caches and exported reports and share them only with authorized
recipients for the disclosed purpose. No evidence-upload service is provided.

Findings are investigative leads. Names, account changes, unsigned modules,
private executable memory, deleted files, history gaps and configuration changes
can have legitimate explanations. Independently corroborate relevant activity,
file identity, timestamps and attribution. Provide an opportunity to explain or
contest findings before taking action. Do not claim the software establishes
guilt, complete coverage or a guaranteed detection/success rate.

Do not use the software for covert surveillance, unauthorized access, harassment,
extortion, evidence fabrication or unlawful discrimination. Do not bypass device
access controls to acquire evidence. Read-only collection does not mean zero
impact: scanning consumes resources, can trigger security software and can cause
normal operating-system access logs or cache activity.

Custom detection rules are the operator's responsibility. Matches are not vetted
identities, and rules must not be used to execute scanned files. Some features
require administrative privileges or optional dependencies; inaccessible or
unsupported checks are limitations, not negative findings. Update integrity
checks do not guarantee a release is free of defects. Warranty, liability,
redistribution, attribution and termination provisions remain in LICENSE.
